@page "/demo-guide"

<PageTitle>Demo Guide - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard demo-guide-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Portfolio Review"
               Title="Demo Guide"
               Subtitle="Guided walkthroughs for reviewing OperationsFlow as a safety/compliance workflow, admin/document workflow, and technical portfolio project.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="safety-meeting-pack">Safety Meeting Pack</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="reports">Reports</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to review OperationsFlow without needing a live explanation. It shows the recommended paths for business users, safety/compliance reviewers, and technical interviewers.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Demo Paths</span>
            <strong>3</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Business, admin, and technical review</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Main Focus</span>
            <strong>Safety</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Compliance follow-up and reporting</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Prototype Type</span>
            <strong>Blazor</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">.NET / EF Core / SQLite</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Review Style</span>
            <strong>Guided</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Click-through portfolio walkthrough</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Safety / Compliance Demo Path</h2>
                    <p>Use this route to show the OSHE-style safety/compliance workflow.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Start with Safety Overview</strong>
                    <span>Review attention items, high/critical risks, expired training, overdue document reviews, and recent compliance activity.</span>
                    <a href="compliance-dashboard">Open Safety Overview</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Open Safety Meeting Pack</strong>
                    <span>Use the meeting-ready summary to review overdue actions, training issues, risks, document reviews, and follow-up points.</span>
                    <a href="safety-meeting-pack">Open Meeting Pack</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Review Compliance Calendar</strong>
                    <span>Check what is overdue, due this week, due in the next 30 days, and coming later.</span>
                    <a href="compliance-calendar">Open Calendar</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Create follow-up from Risk Register</strong>
                    <span>Use a high/critical risk to generate a corrective action with prefilled title, owner, priority, and notes.</span>
                    <a href="risk-register">Open Risk Register</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Review Training Compliance</strong>
                    <span>Check expired or expiring training and generate follow-up corrective actions where needed.</span>
                    <a href="training">Open Training</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Review Document Control</strong>
                    <span>Check overdue/due-soon document reviews and create corrective actions when follow-up is required.</span>
                    <a href="documents">Open Documents</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Export reports</strong>
                    <span>Use the Safety / Compliance Export Pack for CSV reporting, meeting notes, or Excel/Power BI-style analysis.</span>
                    <a href="reports">Open Reports</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Check Activity Log</strong>
                    <span>Confirm record-level traceability for created and updated workflow items.</span>
                    <a href="activity-log">Open Activity Log</a>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Admin / Document Workflow Demo Path</h2>
                    <p>Use this route to show general business workflow and admin process tracking.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Start with Dashboard</strong>
                    <span>Review the overall operational workload and summary cards.</span>
                    <a href="">Open Dashboard</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Open Document Intake</strong>
                    <span>Review incoming document records, assigned owners, target systems, statuses, due dates, and notes.</span>
                    <a href="document-intake">Open Intake</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Update an intake item</strong>
                    <span>Change status or priority to show how incoming work moves through the workflow.</span>
                    <a href="document-intake">Open Intake</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Review Workload</strong>
                    <span>Show owner-based workload, overdue work, and assigned follow-up responsibility.</span>
                    <a href="workload">Open Workload</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Review Reminders</strong>
                    <span>Show upcoming and overdue items that need operational or compliance follow-up.</span>
                    <a href="reminders">Open Reminders</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Open Data Quality</strong>
                    <span>Show missing owners, overdue work, expired training, document review issues, and recommended actions.</span>
                    <a href="data-quality">Open Data Quality</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Export CSVs</strong>
                    <span>Show how the system supports external reporting and analysis workflows.</span>
                    <a href="reports">Open Reports</a>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Technical Interview Demo Path</h2>
                    <p>Use this route to explain the project as a .NET/business-systems portfolio piece.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Explain the stack</strong>
                    <span>Blazor, C#, EF Core, SQLite, Razor components, CSV exports, and local demo data.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Show the workflow model</strong>
                    <span>Work orders, corrective actions, document control, risk, training, document intake, reports, activity log, and data quality.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Show generated corrective actions</strong>
                    <span>Risk, training, and document issues can create prefilled corrective actions.</span>
                    <a href="corrective-actions">Open Corrective Actions</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Show reporting/export logic</strong>
                    <span>CSV exports support Excel/Power BI-style workflows and management reporting.</span>
                    <a href="reports">Open Reports</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Show Data Quality</strong>
                    <span>Business rules identify overdue work, weak records, and missing accountability.</span>
                    <a href="data-quality">Open Data Quality</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Show Activity Log</strong>
                    <span>Activity history demonstrates record-level traceability for workflow changes.</span>
                    <a href="activity-log">Open Activity Log</a>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Explain future upgrade path</strong>
                    <span>Authentication, roles, production database, Microsoft 365 integrations, file storage, API, tests, and deployment.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>About This Prototype</h2>
                    <p>What OperationsFlow is, what it proves, and what it is not pretending to be.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="prototype-scope-grid">
                <article class="prototype-scope-card">
                    <h3>What It Is</h3>
                    <p>
                        OperationsFlow is a Blazor/.NET business workflow prototype for tracking work,
                        corrective actions, safety/compliance issues, document intake, reports, exports,
                        workload, reminders, activity history, and data quality.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="prototype-scope-card">
                    <h3>What It Demonstrates</h3>
                    <p>
                        It demonstrates CRUD workflows, business process modelling, compliance follow-up,
                        CSV exports, record traceability, data quality rules, and portfolio-ready documentation.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="prototype-scope-card">
                    <h3>Prototype Only</h3>
                    <p>
                        This version uses local demo data. It does not yet include production authentication,
                        live Microsoft 365 integrations, hosted deployment, production backups, or secured file storage.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="prototype-scope-card">
                    <h3>Production Upgrade Path</h3>
                    <p>
                        A production version would add user accounts, roles, SQL Server/Azure SQL,
                        SharePoint document storage, Outlook/Teams notifications, API endpoints,
                        automated tests, deployment, and monitoring.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>